      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "1: `ch <- v` unbuffered, reader returned early on an error path.",
            "That is the classic HTTP-handler-with-timeout leak.",
            "2: producer died from a panic or an early return; `range` never ends.",
            "3: the only sender disappears and the goroutine waits out the process."
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Definition",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "A goroutine permanently `_Gwaiting`, or looping with no exit.",
            "Unreachable by any code that could ever finish it.",
            "The GC collects unreachable memory — never a goroutine.",
            "A running goroutine is a GC root by definition."
          ]
        },
